  "id": "Wandsworth-2025_4671",
  "appeal_status": null,
  "appeal_start_date": null,
  "description": "Residential conversion of part existing office rear oancillary storage space  to provide for one studio flat including new external bin storage. Modification to the rear external door and window opening. ",
  "development_type": "Minor dwellings",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - By reason of its design, layout and location, the proposed dwelling would afford future occupiers with a poor standard of accommodation due to the restricted outlook and the lack of satisfactory private amenity space. Furthermore, the application has also failed to demonstrate that the proposed flat would be provided with acceptable internal floor to ceiling heights. As such, the development fails the requirements of policies LP27 adn LP42(D.2) of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023), policy D6 of the London Plan (2021) and the Technical Housing Standards - Nationally Described Space Standard (2015).",
    "Reason : 2 - In dealing with this application the Council has implemented the requirement in the National Planning Policy Framework to make available detailed advice in the form of our statutory policies in the Local Plan as well as offering a full pre application advice service. However, we have been unable to seek solutions to problems as the proposal is clearly contrary to our statutory policies and negotiation could not overcome the reasons for refusal."
  ],
